From 0eec49356139196bfc488a0e026e686bcda3b605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 03:15:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02237/11362] [outer-loop] #1 eval is HIDDEN (replay worthless)
 + #2 step-wise generic explorer built

#1 RESOLVED: competition scores on a PRIVATE set of UNSEEN games (intentionally OOD vs
public mechanics; 'agents must learn not memorize'). So our 11 banked replays score ~0
on the leaderboard -> the generic step-wise solver is the ENTIRE competitive value.
Scoring rewards efficiency: min(human/agent,1)^2 per level.

#2 BUILT: StepwiseExplorer turns batch graph_explore into an event loop the harness
drives one action/turn (graph + RESET-replay navigation + salience candidates +
depth-capped DFS-then-shallowest-frontier). Honest offline measurement (unseen-game
proxy = force-explore the public games from scratch, 6000-action budget): solves 2/11
(lp85 in 11 actions, sp80 in 4338); 9/11 reach L0. Functional but NOT yet competitive
-- from-scratch solving is the open ARC-AGI-3 problem (frontier models <1%). Path to
strength: the SOTA graph-explore ingredients (salience tiers + frontier-distance nav,
partially via E1) and E3 world-model planning (plan in an induced model = few real
actions = solve-rate AND efficiency). Replay path regression-clean (11/11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
